# The image installs its own dependencies from composer.lock, then `COPY . .`
# copies the source on top. Without this file that copy also drags in whatever
# vendor/ happens to exist on the developer's machine, overwriting the one the
# image just installed.
#
# The failure it produces is genuinely misleading: a package is visibly present
# in vendor/, `composer show` lists it, and PHP still reports its classes as not
# found — because the autoloader was regenerated from someone else's install.
vendor/

# Build artefacts and caches. Copying them in makes the image non-reproducible
# and can carry a cached container compiled against different code.
var/
.phpunit.cache/
.php-cs-fixer.cache
public/bundles/

# Local secrets and overrides never belong in an image.
.env.local
.env.*.local
